## ABS

Source: https://github.com/LeCAR-Lab/ABS
Project: https://agile-but-safe.github.io/
Authors: Tairan He, Chong Zhang, Wenli Xiao, Guanqi He, Changliu Liu, Guanya Shi.

The upstream README states that the codebase is under CC BY-NC 4.0, with inherited
licenses from Legged Gym and RSL-RL. This repository adapts the ABS implementation
from Isaac Gym to IsaacLab and adds the BasicNav / VOP-Net / VOP-Nav workflow,
data collection, evaluation, visualization, and runtime tooling. These changes
are maintained by this repository and are not an official upstream release.
The upstream licensing statement was checked on 2026-11-14:
https://github.com/LeCAR-Lab/ABS/blob/main/README.md

### Source correspondence and modifications

The source comparison on 2026-11-14 used upstream commit
9b95329ffb823c15dead02be620ff96938e4d0a3:
https://github.com/LeCAR-Lab/ABS/tree/9b95329ffb823c15dead02be620ff96938e4d0a3
This identifies the comparison baseline, not necessarily the original import
commit or the complete history of each file. Paths below are repository-relative.

| Material in this repository | Corresponding upstream material and modifications |
| --- | --- |
| source/loco_rl/algorithms/ppo.py | training/rsl_rl/rsl_rl/algorithms/ppo.py: retains the PPO implementation, changes imports and policy type references, and removes recurrent-policy support. |
| source/loco_rl/runners/on_policy_runner.py | training/rsl_rl/rsl_rl/runners/on_policy_runner.py: retains the rollout and training loop; changes policy selection, cost logging, iteration accounting, logging and checkpoint handling, and adds VOP metadata. |
| source/loco_rl/storage/rollout_storage.py | training/rsl_rl/rsl_rl/storage/rollout_storage.py: retains transition storage, return/advantage computation and feed-forward minibatches; removes recurrent-state storage and recurrent minibatches. |
| source/loco_rl/modules/basic_nav_actor_critic.py | training/rsl_rl/rsl_rl/modules/actor_critic.py: retains/adapts the Gaussian-policy interface and directly learned std parameterization. The depth/LiDAR encoders and residual feature-fusion network replace the upstream MLP architecture. |
| source/loco_rl/modules/vop_nav_actor_critic.py | Extends the local BasicNav implementation with velocity-interval features; initializes the same directly learned std parameter and inherits the Gaussian-policy methods from BasicNav. |
| source/assets/mdp/rewards.py and source/assets/mdp/reward_math.py | training/legged_gym/legged_gym/envs/base/legged_robot_pos.py: position_target corresponds to _reward_reach_pos_target_soft/tight; heading_target to _reward_reach_heading_target; stalled to _reward_nomove; stand_at_goal to _reward_stand_still_pos; airborne to _reward_fly; agility_reward follows the structure of _reward_velo_dir. Data access is adapted to IsaacLab, with changes to some formulas, posture offsets, thresholds and contact tests. This correspondence does not attribute every function in these local files to ABS. |

The RSL-RL files above are inherited components included in ABS, not a claim
that all of their contents were originally authored by the ABS authors. Existing
ETH Zurich / NVIDIA copyright notices and applicable BSD terms must be retained.
The actor/critic interface correspondence also applies to the local policy
modules even though their network architectures differ from the upstream MLP.

The IsaacLab environment adaptation, source/stage2/ workflow and VOP navigation
extensions are additions or rewrites relative to this ABS baseline. This source
comparison does not establish exclusive authorship, audit other upstream sources,
or verify the provenance or redistribution rights of weights, datasets or assets.

